      "lineNbr": 100,
      "author": {
        "id": 3617594
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-02T19:33:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes. CXX handles that for us. A C++ `std::unique_ptr\u003cstd::string\u003e` is passed across the FFI boundary to become a Rust [`cxx::UniquePtr\u003ccxx::CxxString\u003e`](https://cxx.rs/binding/uniqueptr.html). `cxx::UniquePtr`\u0027s drop implementation calls back into a [C++ function](https://github.com/dtolnay/cxx/blob/e247ca05841d2669b39e07e084f1e0079b71fa2b/src/cxx.cc#L586) that performs the drop.",
      "parentUuid": "6670f041_6b9e665b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 100,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 100,
        "endChar": 55
      },
