      "writtenOn": "2025-01-02T19:33:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Most of the C++ code returns a `TPM_RC` that can represent either success or failure. `TpmError` only represents an error, so it doesn\u0027t really belong on both sides of the FFI boundary.\n\nIMO we can add `repr(transparent)` if we need it but at the moment it doesn\u0027t really make sense.\n\nWhile writing this, I did realize that `TpmError` would be a bit more clear if it wrapped a `NonZeroU32` rather than a `u32`, so I made that change.",
